  "review": {
    "review": "The initiating failure was an unidentified-potion experiment for a levitation room. Decision 2779 (line 8158) staged at dry floor 762. Decisions 2780–2781 tested potions that revealed haste and healing. Decision 2782 (selection 8167, accepted transition 8168) drank unidentified bistre at full health; the clock advanced 27 turns and HP fell from 55 to zero without another selection. Public effects show paralytic gas, repeated paralysis, and an explicit lightning-bolt death message. The attacker is not established. Azure became known as levitation only after death. The selecting chain is rule-preparation through tools/mage_policy.py:1377 to tools/puzzle_supplies.py:899–967. Its bank check verifies nearby terrain and exits, not the ability to act after paralysis. Isolated original-source helper probes admit the recorded bank; they are not reconstructed runtime memory or a replay. No patch is proposed: the missing safety witness is executable identification or verified gas-immunity preparation before testing. The recorded inventory and geometry do not establish either, and a bank veto or speculative relocation alone could replace death with mandatory-discovery exhaustion. Original tests pass (2,053 run, four skipped); no red/green repair claim is made.",
    "learnings": "An empty visible room, full health and walkable exits do not establish safe unidentified-potion testing: paralysis can consume many turns before the next decision. Separate protection of carried potions from protection of the hero, and never treat post-death potion identities as prior knowledge."
